WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.400
Well, I'm going to work.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.050
You've become lazier at work lately, Matthew.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.850
W-well now. Am I not as before?

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.060
Be careful!

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.220
Marilla, after work, can I go out to play?

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.080
All right. I'll give you about 30 minutes.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.050
Don't forget to return on time.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.220
Don't worry!

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.990
Anne had been at Green Gables
for two weeks...

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:27.910
and the news that Matthew and
Marilla had adopted her,

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.980
had spread all over Avonlea.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.270
You must have felt very badly!

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:46.670
Yes. To think someone who didn't get
ill like me, would fall ill for two weeks.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.520
That flu is not to be underestimated.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.280
Oh yes, Marilla.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:56.650
I've been hearing some
surprising things about you.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.830
I don't suppose you are any
more surprised than I am myself.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.870
I'm getting over my surprise now.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.300
It was too bad there was such a mistake.
Couldn't you have sent her back?

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.130
I suppose we could, but we decided not to.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.490
Matthew took a fancy to her.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.410
But Marilla...

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.240
And I must say I like her myself.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.730
Although I admit she has her faults.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.730
The house seems a different place already.
She's a real bright little thing.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:28.290
Wait!

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:34.070
It's a great responsibility
you've taken on yourself.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.850
Especially when you've never had
any experience with children.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:43.660
You don't know much about her or
her real disposition, I suppose.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.900
But I don't want to discourage you.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.670
I'm not feeling discouraged.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:52.580
When I make up my mind to
do a thing it stays made up.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.000
Alright, alright! You are really stubborn!

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:59.040
I'll call her in.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.390
She's here?

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.470
Anne! Anne! Come home!

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.420
Yes!

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.000
What is it, Marilla?

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:23.620
Well, they didn't pick you for your looks,
that's sure and certain.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.020
She's terrible skinny and homely, Marilla.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.500
Come here, child, and let me
have a look at you.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:38.960
Lawful heart, did any one ever see such
freckles? And hair as red as carrots.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.120
Come here, child, I say.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.390
I hate you!

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.670
I hate you! I hate you! I hate you!

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.070
How dare you call me skinny and ugly?

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:56.450
How dare you say I'm
freckled and redheaded?

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:00.050
You are a rude, impolite, unfeeling woman!

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:00.970
Anne!

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.720
How dare you say such things about me?

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.790
How would you like to have
such things said about you?

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:10.730
How would you like to be told
that you are fat and clumsy

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.200
and probably hadn't a spark
of imagination in you?

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.730
I don't care if I do hurt your
feelings by saying so!

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.500
I hope I hurt them.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.500
You have hurt mine worse than
they were ever hurt before

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.280
even by Mrs. Thomas intoxicated husband.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.010
And I'll never forgive you for it, never!

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.630
Did anybody ever see such a temper!

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:38.410
Anne go to your room and
stay there until I come up.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:57.180
Well, I don't envy you
your job bringing that up.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.140
Sorry!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.660
You shouldn't have twitted her
about her looks, Rachel.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.660
Marilla Cuthbert, you don't mean
to say that you are upholding her

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.660
in such a terrible display of
temper as we've just seen?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:13.370
No, she's been very naughty and I'll have
to give her a talking to about it.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:18.990
But we must make allowances for her.
She's never been taught what is right.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.640
And you were too hard on her, Rachel.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:27.580
Well, I see that I'll have to be very
careful what I say after this,

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.580
since the fine feelings of orphans

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.410
have to be considered before anything else.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.800
Oh, no, I'm not vexed.
Don't worry yourself.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:39.440
I'm too sorry for you to leave any
room for anger in my mind.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.100
You'll have your own troubles with that child.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.580
But if you'll take my advice,

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:48.100
I've brought up ten children and buried two.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:51.630
You'll do that 'talking to' you
mention with a fair-sized birch switch.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:55.070
I should think that would be the most
effective language for that child.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:56.840
Well, good evening.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.870
I hope you'll come down to
see me often as usual, Marilla.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.240
But don't expect me to
visit here again in a hurry

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:10.540
if I'm liable to be flown at and
insulted in such a fashion.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:16.720
It's something new in my experience.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:45.340
Anne.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:47.830
Anne!

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:54.810
Get off that bed this minute and listen
to what I have to say to you.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:04.950
This is a nice way for you to behave. Anne!

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:06.680
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:11.360
She hadn't any right to call
me ugly and redheaded.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:18.790
You hadn't any right to fly into such a
fury and talk the way you did to her.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.560
I was ashamed of you.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:25.560
I'm sure I don't know why you
should lose your temper like that

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.860
just because Mrs. Lynde said you
were red-haired and homely.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.930
You say it yourself often enough.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.500
But there's such a difference
between saying a thing yourself

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.030
and hearing other people say it.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:45.500
You may know a thing is so, but you can't
help hoping other people don't think it is.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:51.700
When she said those things something
just rose right up in me and choked me.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.270
I had to fly out at her.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:57.550
Well, you made a fine exhibition
of yourself I must say.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.480
Mrs. Lynde will have a nice story
to tell about you everywhere.

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:02.480
But...

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:07.460
But, just imagine how you would feel if
somebody told you to your face

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.550
that you were skinny and ugly.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.960
What a pity.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:17.070
She is such a dark, homely little thing.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.960
Marilla is listening!

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:27.970
I don't say that I think Mrs. Lynde was
exactly right in saying what she did to you,

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:34.130
but that is no excuse for such behavior on
your part to a stranger and elderly person.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.100
So, Anne...

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:40.700
You must go to Mrs. Lynde and tell her
you are very sorry for your

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.380
bad temper and ask her to forgive you.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.170
I can never do that!

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.460
I just can´t.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:50.310
You can punish me in any way you like.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:53.520
You can shut me up in a dark, damp
dungeon inhabited by snakes and toads

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.670
and feed me only on bread and water.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:58.930
But I cannot ask her to forgive me.

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.830
We're not in the habit of shutting
people up in dark damp dungeons.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.530
But apologize to Mrs. Lynde
you must and shall

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:07.730
and you'll stay here in your room until
you can tell me you're willing to do it.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.910
I shall have to stay here forever then,

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.640
because I can't tell Mrs. Lynde
I'm sorry I said those things to her.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:18.010
How can I? I'm not sorry.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.200
I'm sorry I've vexed you...

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.940
but I'm glad I told her just what I did.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.520
It was a great satisfaction.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.320
I can't say I'm sorry when I'm not, can I?

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.390
I can't even imagine I'm sorry.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:38.310
Perhaps your imagination will be in
better working order by the morning.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.550
You'll have the night to
think over your conduct in.

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:47.560
You said you would try to be a very
good girl if we kept you at Green Gables,

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.710
but I must say it hasn't seemed
very much like it this evening.

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:26.250
But Anne was not entirely at fault.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:30.930
It's a good thing she gave a calling
down to that meddlesome old gossip.

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:32.840
Matthew, I'm astonished at you.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:37.410
You know that Anne's behavior
was dreadful, and yet you take her part!

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:41.050
I suppose you'll be saying next thing
that she oughtn't to be punished at all!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:45.740
Well now... no... not exactly...

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:48.300
I reckon she ought to be punished a little.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:54.040
That's right. She'll stay up there until she's
willing to apologize.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:01.110
Why do women act like this?

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.110
Did you say something?

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.850
N-no... nothing...

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:44.530
I don't know how long do you intend to
be like that. But you've got to eat.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:48.430
You didn't eat your breakfast or lunch.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.650
I can't eat.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:13:00.400
Do as you wish, but don't think
I'll spare you because of this.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.430
Yes!

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:04.770
Of course you wont let me
go and I shall not complain.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:09.060
I am prepared to stay here all my life.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:05.760
I don't want to do what Rachel says.
But her temper really vexes me.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:09.330
Well, I have to get the cow back.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:57.690
Anne!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.430
How are you making it, Anne?

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.300
Oh, it's you Matthew.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.490
Pretty well.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:11.230
I imagine a good deal,
and that helps to pass the time.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.640
Of course, it's rather lonesome.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.620
But I'll get used to that.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:30.900
Well now, Anne, don't you think you'd
better do it and have it over with?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.970
Marilla's a dreadful determined woman,
dreadful determined.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.780
Do you mean apologize to Mrs. Lynde?

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:40.420
Yes, apologize. That's the very word.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:48.310
Just... smooth it over so to speak.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:55.310
I suppose I could do it to oblige you.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:58.890
It would be true enough to say I am sorry,

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:02.320
because I am sorry now.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:07.370
I wasn't a bit sorry last night.
I was mad clear through.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:16.150
I know I was, because I woke up three times
and I was just furious every time.

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:22.530
But this morning it was over.
I wasn't in a temper anymore.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:26.130
I felt so ashamed of myself.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:31.040
But I just couldn't think of going
and telling Mrs. Lynde so.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.590
It would be so humiliating.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:41.000
I made up my mind I'd stay shut up here
forever rather than do that.

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:45.260
But still...

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.970
I'd do anything for you...

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:52.330
if you really want me to...

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:55.700
Well now, of course I do.

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:59.870
It's terrible lonesome downstairs without you.

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:02.610
Very well.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.850
I'll tell Marilla as soon as
she comes in I've repented.

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:09.680
That's right, that's right.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.000
Don't tell Marilla I said anything about it.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:19.430
Don't worry.
Wild horses won't drag the secret from me.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.420
You're here already, Matthew?

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.470
I just came back.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.210
Right, I have to sow the seeds.

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.090
Why was he so flustered?

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:08.440
Marilla.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:10.900
Well?

00:18:11.970 --> 00:18:15.370
I'm sorry I lost my temper
and said rude things.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:20.640
I'm willing to go and tell Mrs. Lynde so.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:21.750
Very well.

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:24.640
Arrange your hair, and we'll be off.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.210
What are you thinking of?

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:20.090
I'm imagining out what I
must say to Mrs. Lynde.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:25.390
But why doesn't your face seem to suggest so?

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:47.590
Oh, Mrs. Lynde, I am so extremely sorry.
I could never express all my sorrow.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:52.470
No, not if I used up a whole dictionary.

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:56.790
You must just imagine it.

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.220
I behaved terribly to you,

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.140
and I've disgraced the dear friends

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:06.090
Matthew and Marilla, who have
let me stay at Green Gables.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.340
I'm a dreadfully wicked
and ungrateful girl,

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:15.330
and I deserve to be punished and cast out
by respectable people forever.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:21.110
It was very wicked of me to fly into a
temper because you told me the truth.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:23.920
Every word you said was true.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:29.930
My hair is red and I'm freckled
and skinny and ugly.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.220
What I said to you was true, too...

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:35.760
but I shouldn't have said it.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:41.570
Oh, Mrs. Lynde, please, please, forgive me.

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:46.980
If you refuse it will be a
lifelong sorrow on me.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:52.350
would you put this suffering
on a poor little orphan girl,

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:55.350
even if she had a dreadful temper?

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:59.530
Oh, I am sure you wouldn't.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:03.420
Please say you forgive me, Mrs. Lynde.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:19.110
There, there, get up, child.
Of course I forgive you.

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:22.510
I guess I was a little too hard on you,
anyway. You just mustn't mind me.

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:26.790
It can't be denied your hair is terrible red, but

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:30.790
I knew a girl once whose hair was every mite
as red as yours when she was young

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:34.000
but when she grew up it darkened
to a real handsome auburn.

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.970
I wouldn't be a mite surprised if yours did, too.

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:41.820
Oh, Mrs. Lynde! You have given me a hope.

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:45.120
Oh, I could endure anything if I only thought

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:49.330
my hair would be a handsome
auburn when I grew up.

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:54.110
It would be so much easier to be good if
one's hair was a handsome auburn.

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:58.400
Oh Mrs. Lynde, I shall always feel
that you are a benefactor.

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:02.440
Your temper's pretty quick, I guess,
but there's one comfort.

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:06.480
A child that has a quick temper, ain't
never likely to be sly or deceitful.

00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:07.560
Don't you think, Marilla?

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:14.940
I don't feel so surprised at
you keeping her as I did.

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:42.210
I apologized pretty well, didn't I?

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:44.580
You did it thoroughly, all right enough.

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:48.460
I thought since I had to do it, I
might as well do it thoroughly.

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:53.420
Marilla, do you suppose my hair will really
be a handsome auburn when I grow up?

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:58.030
You shouldn't think so much
about your looks, Anne.

00:22:58.340 --> 00:23:01.320
I'm afraid you are a very vain little girl.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:05.600
How can I be vain when I know I'm homely?

00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:08.560
I love pretty things.

00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:13.070
Handsome is as handsome does.

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:17.440
I've had that said to me before,
but I have my doubts about it.

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:42.080
It's lovely to be going home
and know it's home.

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:46.580
Oh, Marilla, I'm so happy.

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:52.450
Something warm and pleasant welled up

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:56.570
in Marilla's heart at touch of
that thin little hand in her own.

00:23:57.370 --> 00:24:02.860
A throb of the maternity
she had missed, perhaps.

00:24:16.580 --> 00:24:20.800
Sunday, Marilla got Anne to the church.

00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:24.190
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:24.780 --> 00:24:27.350
Anne's Impressions of Sunday-School

00:24:27.470 --> 00:24:28.510
Please watch!
